WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.271
There is a common expectation that adopting more
advanced or expressive architectures

00:00:05.351 --> 00:00:07.537
will inherently improve calibration.

00:00:07.617 --> 00:00:11.880
Through a controlled case study on a structural
distortion benchmark,

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:17.797
the authors demonstrate this expectation is false:
graph transformers and positional encodings

00:00:17.877 --> 00:00:22.707
do not meaningfully improve calibration over
vanilla message-passing networks,

00:00:22.787 --> 00:00:26.358
and increasing model size can even make calibration worse.

00:00:26.438 --> 00:00:28.876
This finding motivates a different path.

00:00:28.956 --> 00:00:30.953
Rather than chasing expressivity,

00:00:31.033 --> 00:00:37.500
the paper advocates for epistemic uncertainty
quantification to directly modulate confidence indicators.
